<h2>Advanced Use — Tools, Workflows, Windows</h2>
<p>OMC provides a family of tools for handling code more precisely. They are useful when you need analysis more precise than a text search.</p>

<div class="tbl-wrap">
    <table>
        <thead>
            <tr><th>Tool family</th><th>Representative features</th><th>What it is used for</th><th>Cautions</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr><td><strong>LSP</strong></td><td>lsp_hover, lsp_goto_definition, lsp_find_references, lsp_diagnostics</td><td>Accurate symbol navigation, checking type errors, searching references</td><td>Requires a per-language server such as typescript-language-server, pyright, or rust-analyzer</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>AST Grep</strong></td><td>ast_grep_search, ast_grep_replace</td><td>Search · replace based on syntactic structure</td><td>More precise than a text grep, but you need the skill to write the patterns</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Python REPL</strong></td><td>Analysis based on pandas, numpy, matplotlib</td><td>CSV · log · statistical analysis</td><td>You need to check access permissions for the data files and package availability</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Ask / Team CLI</strong></td><td>omc ask, omc team, omc session search</td><td>External CLI workers and session search</td><td>You need to distinguish the plugin installation flow from the CLI/runtime path</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
</div>

<div class="note">
    <span class="nh">A note on LSP</span>
    LSP (Language Server Protocol) is a standard that helps a code editor accurately work out "where is this variable defined?" and "is there a type error here?". Note, though, that the language server for the language in question must be installed for it to work properly.
</div>

<h3>Workflows by Real-World Scenario</h3>
<p>We have organized how modes, agents, and tools are woven together in real situations into eight scenarios. Use the number buttons or the previous/next buttons below to look through the scenarios one at a time.</p>

