        <div class="scn">
            <h4>Scenario 2 — adding a feature</h4>
            <p>If the requirements are clear, go straight to autopilot; if they are vague, refine them with deep-interview first and then implement.</p>
            <pre><code><span class="c"># When the requirements are clear</span>
autopilot: add email notification features (signup welcome, password reset, order confirmation)
<span class="c"># When the requirements are vague — clarify first</span>
/deep-interview "add a notification feature"
<span class="c"># → implement with the clarified requirements</span>
autopilot: implement with [the clarified requirements]</code></pre>
        </div>

        <div class="scn">
            <h4>Scenario 3 — refactoring legacy code</h4>
            <p>Proceed safely in four steps: grasp the current state → plan → parallel conversion → verification.</p>
